# AI-Native Evaluations → Idea Backlog

Pointers to per-repo AI-native evaluation docs. Each eval rates the codebase across 10 dimensions and has a "highest-leverage fix" column — those are pre-scoped PR-sized ideas waiting to be promoted.

## Per-repo evals

- **\<repo-1\>** — `<path to eval doc>`
- **\<repo-2\>** — `<path to eval doc>`

## Dimensions rated

1. Agent entry points (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, rules)
2. Verifiability (smoke commands, test speed)
3. Discoverability (conventions, predictable structure)
4. Explicit contracts (shared types, schema enforcement)
5. Context-efficient docs (focused, ADRs, no stale clutter)
6. Repeatable workflows (.claude/skills, .claude/agents)
7. Safety guardrails (allowlists, hooks, migration locks)
8. Codebase hygiene (lint strictness, file size limits, cruft)
9. Observability & repro (error tracking, metrics, repro harness)
10. Environment & first-run (setup scripts, env.example completeness)

## How COS uses this

The **ai-native idea generator** (self-build item #6) reads these evals, scans the "highest-leverage fix" columns, and writes `ideas` rows with `source=generator:ai-native` and a confidence score. Each idea's title/description references the specific dimension and fix.

## Cadence

Re-run the eval quarterly. Diff against the prior eval — the delta is what shipped and what regressed.
